L000945	\subsection{Capacitance calibration for the dual-gate TME setup}
L000946	
L000947	For the dual-gate TME setup, the relevant capacitances are $C_\text{TG}$, $C_\text{BG}$, the parasitic capacitances of the two gate lines, and the sample geometric capacitance $C_\text{S}$. The overlap capacitance analogous to $C_\text{p1}$ can be estimated from the device geometry and is neglected here.
L000948	
L000949	The gate capacitances $C_\text{TG}$ and $C_\text{BG}$, together with the corresponding parasitic capacitances, can be calibrated in the same way as in the single-gate case by tuning the sample surface to the coercive-field region and fitting the linear frequency dependence of the imaginary current.
L000950	
L000951	The sample geometric capacitance $C_\text{S}$ is calibrated separately in the axion-insulator state, where the sample is insulating. An AC voltage is applied to one gate and the current is measured in the other gate line, so that the line parasitic capacitances do not contribute. The measured total capacitance ($C_\text{total}$) then satisfies
L000952	\begin{equation}
L000953	C_\text{total}^{-1}=(C_\text{TG}^{(\text{geo})})^{-1}+(C_\text{BG}^{(\text{geo})})^{-1}+C_\text{S}^{-1} \approx C_\text{TG}^{-1}+C_\text{BG}^{-1}+C_\text{S}^{-1},
L000954	\label{eq:SM_Cs_calibration}
L000955	\end{equation}
L000956	from which $C_\text{S}$ is obtained.
L000957	
L000958	\section{Additional data of QAH charge accumulation compensation}
